  "traitsSource": "ESTIMATED: the direction of each pull follows research on personality and word use (Mehl, Gosling and Pennebaker 2006, 'Personality in its natural habitat', JPSP 90(5); Yarkoni 2010, 'Personality in 100,000 words', J. Research in Personality 44(3)): extraverted and agreeable people talk more and warmer, neurotic people hedge, disagreeable people argue. Sizes are TUNABLE, spread -1 to 1 each; the owner's trait-fit grades move them. The people-mind traits every person carries (sociability, conflict, deliberation, risk, reliability) and the facets officials are drawn with (duty-bound, enterprising, practical) pull the same way: outgoing toward warm and longer, quarrelsome toward braced, deliberate toward calm, bold away from guarded."
